  "methods": [
    "Opposing principal-axis rays sampled 25 cheek sections and 25 floor-to-roof sections per pocket in both binary STLs and both placed viewer meshes. Nine insertion paths ran through each mouth to the blind stop. Two probes located the stock face at each mouth.",
    "The enclosure results use appliance coordinates. The lid results use lid STL coordinates after reversing its placement in the complete assembly. The six ceiling-down rear wells retain the one-sided 0.25 mm roof relief within the stated opening. Their long-axis centres are 0.125 mm below the installed connector datums. The lid apertures are centred on their connector datums.",
    "The stop gap uses the unchanged connector pose, the molded rear face and the measured stop. Short and long dimensions describe the fitted grip. The WAGO 221-413 purchased reference has a nominal envelope of 8.4 by 18.8 mm in those directions.",
    "For each complete STL, identical triangles were matched by their three stored vertices. Every unpaired triangle was planar on a principal axis. Polygon intersections measured the before-only and after-only area on each plane outside all old and new pocket bounds. Signed volume and 86 nearby stock rays per pocket were checked independently.",
    "Each current print-region record names the measured STL. Its removable tree bounds coincide with the measured cavity and its roof bridge crosses the short span onto both solid cheeks. The 0.25 mm automatic-support blocker overrun on the back and lid is outside the physical aperture. These region comparisons use authored geometry."
  ],
